module

public import CORALean.ContSet.Zonotope.Real.Operations.Face
public import CORALean.ContSet.Zonotope.Real.Theorems.MemArgmaxIff

@[expose] public section

/-!
# Every exposed face of a zonotope is the zonotope of a subset of its generators

The exposed face of `Z = c + ∑ βⱼgⱼ, |βⱼ| ≤ 1` in direction `u`, the points of `Z` maximizing `u`,
is exactly `c + ∑_{u gⱼ ≠ 0} sign(u gⱼ)gⱼ + Z(gⱼ | u gⱼ = 0)`, the zonotope `Z.face u`: the
coefficients of the generators `u` does not annihilate are pinned to signs (`mem_argmax_iff`), the
others are free. So "if `F` is a face of a zonotope generated by `Γ`, then `F` is a zonotope
generated by some `Γ′ ⊆ Γ`" [1, Sec. 3 (faces)], for every functional `u`, `u = 0` giving `Z`
itself. Termwise, `βⱼgⱼ = sign(u gⱼ)gⱼ + βⱼ(Z.face u).Gⱼ` for coefficients pinned off the
annihilated generators, which is the whole proof in both directions.

## Inputs
* `Z` – zonotope
* `u` – linear functional

## Hypotheses
* none

## Conclusion
* the face zonotope is the set of maximizers of `u`

## References

* [1] M. Černý. "Goffin's algorithm for zonotopes". Kybernetika, 48(5):890-906, 2012.
-/

